{
 "_doc": "Tier-3 living Ashen camp in the high timber (ADR-0048): the watch camp's kit (palisade, longhouse, lean-to, smoke huts, pyre, effigies; shells round small kit rooms under roof 'none') plus the living camp's own props (props/ashen.json: war drum, spear racks, ash pots, drying racks, fed camp fires). Its fires burn (lit + keep, lights_on 1). The camp's people are not sleepers: the AshenDirector spawns them awake round the fires (data/factions/ashen.json camps). The only sleepers are three 'taken' Ashen the camp keeps chained in the binding hut (population ashen). Route: the trail -> the open gateway between two fires -> the big fire and the drum -> the binding hut's chained door (jaws in the grass before it; its key hangs over a bed in the lean-to; opening or breaking the chain, or the jaws' snap, sets the taken loose) -> the smoke hut for the cache key -> the longhouse through the hide-hung hole in its east wall (bone chimes across it: an alarm) -> the hatch to the cache pit -> the longhouse's bolted back door out through the palisade line. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
 "_ashen": "A living camp (ADR-0048): residents come from the AshenDirector, not from this file. Keep sleepers to the taken; the camp's fires and pyre are lit props and register as the camp's own fires (they don't scare their own people).",
