   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "story": "The Ashen came up here the first winter, when the valley below turned. From the rise they can see the river road, the convoy road and the smoke of anyone who lights a fire, and somebody is always watching. The drum by the gate calls the camp; the fires are never let die, and the dead go on the pyre the same night. They live off the timber and off whoever comes up the river road with something worth taking: a Remand salvager's pack, a trader's cart, a drop canister out of the sky. They don't take the sick. When three of their own turned in the spring - one of them clawed through the longhouse's east wall on the way out - they couldn't bring themselves to burn them. They chained them in the small hut by the east wall instead, and every night the woman who keeps the key to the chain sits outside the door and sings to them.",
